FSL-derived reference data
--------------------------

Two reference images in container/scripts/ are derivatives of FSL
standard-space data. They are versioned in this repository, rather than
rebuilt during the image build, because the numbers this pipeline produces
depend on their exact contents and neither is reproducible from a build-time
recipe: resampling afresh yields a subtly different image, and the skeleton
mask encodes method decisions that no recipe captures.

  - FMRIB58_FA_2mm_crop.nii.gz
    A 2mm-resampled and cropped derivative of FMRIB58_FA_1mm.nii.gz. It is
    the initial target for the within-subject ANTs template construction
    used on longitudinal (multi-timepoint) runs.

  - delta-svd_skeletonmask_v1.nii.gz
    A masked subset of FMRIB58_FA-skeleton_1mm.nii.gz on the same 1mm grid,
    restricting the analysed skeleton to the tracts this method evaluates.

No FSL software is redistributed in this source repository -- only these two
derived reference images. Condition (3) above concerns source code; these are
image data, for which no source code exists and none is therefore withheld.
